WEBVTT


00:01:31.728 --> 00:01:34.267
- Hello, Auntie.
- Hi, how are you?

00:01:34.267 --> 00:01:35.824
Did Weechana go to see you?

00:01:35.824 --> 00:01:38.454
That's right. He came to see me.

00:01:38.454 --> 00:01:40.992
So many people asked to take photos with him.

00:01:40.992 --> 00:01:44.120
He didn't know
you wanted to break up with him, right?

00:01:45.451 --> 00:01:47.616
We haven't had a serious conversation
about it yet.

00:01:47.616 --> 00:01:50.646
Listen, if he invites you somewhere,
don't go with him.

00:01:50.646 --> 00:01:52.395
Call me first if he does.

00:01:52.395 --> 00:01:55.239
Why? What's the matter?

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:56.940
Is everything okay?

00:01:57.683 --> 00:01:59.800
I'll call you later.

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:01.560
I need to go now.

00:02:07.011 --> 00:02:09.200
He did visit my aunt.

00:02:10.678 --> 00:02:12.680
Why would he do that?

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:16.560
Eva,

00:02:16.566 --> 00:02:18.960
I secretly recorded you and Weechana
the other day...

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:24.239
while you two were arguing.

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:25.734
What?

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:31.662
Here.

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:34.040
Wasn't I the one

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:36.959
who helped you become
a top-tier actress like this?

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:40.659
I have agreed to serve as your accessory
in this industry.

00:02:40.659 --> 00:02:43.190
And I have agreed to be your supporter
for a long time.

00:02:43.190 --> 00:02:44.664
What's the problem with that?

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:47.886
It wasn't a total loss to be beside me,
was it?

00:02:47.886 --> 00:02:49.347
You were merely a food vendor.

00:02:49.347 --> 00:02:51.864
You need to help me with my campaign.

00:02:52.579 --> 00:02:55.040
And you need to drive the damn car!

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:04.443
Well, I...

00:03:04.443 --> 00:03:05.519
Right.

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:08.219
Follow his lead and help with the campaign.

00:03:08.219 --> 00:03:10.251
Just do whatever he tells you to do.

00:03:10.251 --> 00:03:13.160
So you two can part on good terms.

00:03:14.442 --> 00:03:17.382
But if you ever feel like you're in danger,

00:03:17.382 --> 00:03:19.360
we'll release the video immediately.

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:23.161
I believe social media will be on our side.

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:38.960
[Grandma Jit]
What?

00:03:41.723 --> 00:03:42.680
Hello, Grandma.

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:45.032
I need to talk to you.

00:03:45.032 --> 00:03:47.544
I'll send someone to pick you up
this afternoon.

00:03:48.857 --> 00:03:53.611
I... I need to... work out for my role
in the film.

00:03:53.611 --> 00:03:55.477
It won't take long,

00:03:55.477 --> 00:03:58.997
and Weechana can't find out about this.

00:04:14.216 --> 00:04:15.576
Baby.

00:04:15.576 --> 00:04:17.377
Baby!

00:04:18.883 --> 00:04:21.189
Did your brother buy Eva a new car?

00:04:23.936 --> 00:04:26.102
He did?

00:04:26.102 --> 00:04:28.309
I want a new one, too.

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:33.365
Eva wanted to break up with him.

00:04:33.365 --> 00:04:34.800
What?

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.483
Why?

00:04:38.181 --> 00:04:39.989
I don't know.

00:04:41.019 --> 00:04:43.568
Dad must have him send her a car
to make it up to her.

00:04:43.568 --> 00:04:45.549
Oh, my God!

00:04:47.569 --> 00:04:49.370
Should we do the same?

00:04:52.395 --> 00:04:54.005
What do you mean?

00:04:54.005 --> 00:04:57.699
Tell your dad that we're breaking up

00:04:57.699 --> 00:04:59.749
so he'll buy me a new car.

00:05:02.747 --> 00:05:04.997
Baby, listen.

00:05:06.144 --> 00:05:08.453
If you ask Grandma for a new car,

00:05:08.453 --> 00:05:10.931
she will definitely buy one for you.

00:05:13.437 --> 00:05:14.991
You're right.

00:05:19.325 --> 00:05:21.277
Eva had some nerve doing this.

00:05:21.277 --> 00:05:23.384
She came from nothing.

00:05:23.384 --> 00:05:26.349
Still, she was so dramatic
about trying to break up with him.

00:05:29.989 --> 00:05:32.489
It looks like Weechana
is really in love with her.

00:05:33.613 --> 00:05:34.952
You think?

00:05:35.915 --> 00:05:37.327
But...

00:05:41.089 --> 00:05:44.805
not as much as he loves himself.

00:05:44.805 --> 00:05:47.149
Grandma doesn't like her at all.

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:49.749
I don't think they will make it.

00:06:23.187 --> 00:06:26.173
Mom! I'm back.

00:06:26.173 --> 00:06:29.029
Mom? Mom?

00:06:30.211 --> 00:06:32.424
Mom, where are you?

00:06:32.424 --> 00:06:34.225
Mom?

00:06:37.901 --> 00:06:39.524
Mom?

00:06:41.069 --> 00:06:42.870
Mom?

00:06:54.928 --> 00:06:59.749
My dearest son,
I need to go abroad for a while

00:06:59.749 --> 00:07:02.944
because I have a lot to take care of.

00:07:02.944 --> 00:07:05.589
I'm sorry that I couldn't hug you goodbye.

00:07:05.589 --> 00:07:10.735
Be nice to your dad and your grandma
when I am not around.

00:07:10.735 --> 00:07:12.789
You have to behave around your grandma.

00:07:12.789 --> 00:07:17.696
I'll get back to you as soon as I can.

00:07:17.696 --> 00:07:21.816
No matter what happens,

00:07:21.816 --> 00:07:24.149
always remember that I love you.

00:07:33.472 --> 00:07:35.273
Can I have some coffee?

00:07:47.923 --> 00:07:49.989
You look so much like your mom.

00:07:51.517 --> 00:07:54.389
If you were a woman,
I'm sure you'd be beautiful.

00:07:59.125 --> 00:08:02.335
When will my brother ask you and your friends
to come to his office?

00:08:03.148 --> 00:08:04.341
Tomorrow.

00:08:04.341 --> 00:08:07.787
He'll brief us on his campaign strategy

00:08:07.787 --> 00:08:10.829
and the guidelines for using social media
to support him.

00:08:11.739 --> 00:08:16.875
Good, I'll stop by tomorrow.

00:08:32.669 --> 00:08:36.256
That's great. You need to do it slowly
and feel your muscles.

00:08:36.256 --> 00:08:38.592
Tuck your elbows in,
keeping them close to your body.

00:08:38.592 --> 00:08:41.438
Breathe out as you lift.

00:08:41.438 --> 00:08:43.987
That's it, and lower the bar slowly.

00:08:43.987 --> 00:08:46.669
Keep your elbows steady, that's right.

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:49.861
You're doing great. Focus.

00:08:49.861 --> 00:08:53.195
Pun, can I talk to you for a minute?

00:08:53.195 --> 00:08:56.373
- Sure.
- Eva's schedule is getting busy this month.

00:08:56.373 --> 00:09:00.205
I need to scale back her workout plan
from what we originally planned.

00:09:00.205 --> 00:09:04.709
She also needs to go somewhere
this afternoon.

00:09:05.395 --> 00:09:07.229
Campaigning for him?

00:09:07.229 --> 00:09:10.147
Does Eva need to help with his campaign?

00:09:10.147 --> 00:09:11.551
Yes, she does.

00:09:14.266 --> 00:09:16.043
She asked me to reduce her workout schedule.

00:09:21.811 --> 00:09:23.621
Oh my!

00:09:23.621 --> 00:09:28.612
Does she only have two hours
to train with me on those days?

00:09:28.612 --> 00:09:29.807
Yeah.

00:09:29.807 --> 00:09:31.661
I can only train until 11 today.

00:09:31.661 --> 00:09:33.616
Should we get back to work?

00:09:33.616 --> 00:09:35.781
You're not giving us enough time,

00:09:35.781 --> 00:09:39.829
so don't be surprised by the results.

00:09:44.304 --> 00:09:49.819
I guess... we can push harder at the end.

00:09:49.819 --> 00:09:53.173
If this is your solution to this,

00:09:53.173 --> 00:09:55.549
then do whatever you want.

00:09:56.251 --> 00:09:57.941
Coach, what do you think?

00:09:57.941 --> 00:10:01.136
We have three hours to spare today.

00:10:01.136 --> 00:10:02.824
What should we do with the extra time?

00:10:02.824 --> 00:10:05.464
There's so much to do that we can't decide.

00:10:05.464 --> 00:10:07.789
What is wrong with you?

00:10:07.789 --> 00:10:09.009
I only asked you to reduce the training time.

00:10:09.009 --> 00:10:10.760
I never asked you to lower your rate.

00:10:10.760 --> 00:10:12.349
I have something important to do.

00:10:12.349 --> 00:10:15.101
I only asked you to adjust
my training program to fit my schedule.

00:10:15.101 --> 00:10:16.547
It's not that difficult.

00:10:16.547 --> 00:10:19.629
Your training program
wasn't put together randomly.

00:10:20.952 --> 00:10:24.389
Your daily workout plan
needs to be structured

00:10:24.389 --> 00:10:27.469
and work together
with the meal plan I prepared.

00:10:27.469 --> 00:10:29.344
They go hand in hand.

00:10:29.344 --> 00:10:31.759
If you can't stick to the plan,

00:10:31.759 --> 00:10:36.590
you'll have to deal with the consequences.

00:10:37.787 --> 00:10:41.147
Alright, it's fine. That's okay.

00:10:41.147 --> 00:10:45.489
Let me take another look at your schedule
and see what we can do.

00:10:46.861 --> 00:10:48.872
What about your script?

00:10:48.872 --> 00:10:52.957
You're still confused about the basics:
"I", "you", "we", and "they".

00:10:52.957 --> 00:10:55.589
But you prioritized your boyfriend's campaign
over this one?

00:10:56.733 --> 00:11:00.429
You have too many difficult tasks to handle
in such a short time.

00:11:02.344 --> 00:11:04.131
You still can't make time for yourself.

00:11:04.131 --> 00:11:05.629
Pun.

00:11:05.629 --> 00:11:07.909
Can I talk to you for a minute?

00:11:11.904 --> 00:11:13.462
Pun.

00:11:24.856 --> 00:11:26.792
Eva is a sensitive person.

00:11:26.792 --> 00:11:29.884
She may look strong on the outside,
but she's so soft on the inside.

00:11:29.884 --> 00:11:33.005
She's been dealing with so much lately,
and it's not good for her.

00:11:33.005 --> 00:11:35.000
Could you please go easy on her?

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:37.389
I'm just worried that her plan won't work.

00:11:38.405 --> 00:11:41.221
The producer wants to check
her dialogue delivery and accent next week.

00:11:41.221 --> 00:11:44.304
And she needs to be physically ready
for fight training next month.

00:11:44.304 --> 00:11:47.115
You said you didn't have time,

00:11:47.115 --> 00:11:48.475
and that's not good for anyone.

00:11:48.475 --> 00:11:51.557
Trust me, we don't want this either,

00:11:51.557 --> 00:11:53.349
but it is what it is.

00:11:53.349 --> 00:11:54.958
Damn it!

00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:58.320
Pun.

00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:03.888
Trust me,
Eva doesn't like this situation either,

00:12:03.888 --> 00:12:06.221
but there's nothing we can do about it.

00:12:06.221 --> 00:12:09.741
Please understand and support her.

00:12:09.741 --> 00:12:12.039
That's all I'm asking of you.

00:12:13.912 --> 00:12:15.341
Fine.

00:12:29.779 --> 00:12:31.709
Listen,

00:12:32.461 --> 00:12:34.803
if you don't like the way he treated you,
you can tell me.

00:12:34.803 --> 00:12:38.299
I can find someone else. We still have time.

00:12:38.299 --> 00:12:40.992
Do you remember
the strengths I told you about?

00:12:41.867 --> 00:12:44.005
He's so focused on his work

00:12:44.005 --> 00:12:46.989
and he doesn't treat me differently
because of who I am.

00:12:47.819 --> 00:12:52.016
Actually, he was right about everything.

00:12:53.317 --> 00:12:55.328
He was right.

00:12:55.328 --> 00:12:58.254
I know he meant well,

00:12:58.254 --> 00:13:00.829
but he didn't have to say it like that.

00:13:00.829 --> 00:13:03.283
He didn't have
to yell at you like that, either.

00:13:08.307 --> 00:13:09.981
I need you to adjust my training program.

00:13:09.981 --> 00:13:11.344
What?

00:13:12.333 --> 00:13:14.845
I still need my training program
added back to my schedule.

00:13:15.672 --> 00:13:16.944
What?

00:13:16.944 --> 00:13:19.136
But you'll be campaigning all day.

00:13:19.136 --> 00:13:20.629
It'll be too exhausting for you.

00:13:20.629 --> 00:13:22.469
You'll have to keep waving, smiling,

00:13:22.469 --> 00:13:24.759
and saying hi to people all day,
even under the hot sun.

00:13:24.760 --> 00:13:26.493
I'm going to be fine.

00:13:26.493 --> 00:13:28.136
He was right.

00:13:28.136 --> 00:13:31.773
Preparation is important to me,
and I need to focus on it fully.

00:13:31.773 --> 00:13:33.401
I need to get this part.

00:13:45.093 --> 00:13:46.853
Hey, Pun.

00:13:47.672 --> 00:13:50.307
I understand
that this will disrupt our original plan,

00:13:50.307 --> 00:13:54.707
but she's the one who hired us.

00:13:55.341 --> 00:13:57.109
I know.

00:13:58.253 --> 00:14:01.189
I really admire your dedication to this job.

00:14:02.275 --> 00:14:04.669
If that's what she wants,

00:14:04.669 --> 00:14:06.749
we need to respect her decision.

00:14:07.685 --> 00:14:09.669
- You're right.
- Yeah?

00:14:11.168 --> 00:14:13.739
Come on, you should apologize to her.

00:14:13.739 --> 00:14:15.549
You're too hot-headed.

00:14:20.053 --> 00:14:22.229
- I'm sorry for...
- No need to.

00:14:23.616 --> 00:14:26.112
Go ahead. Keep insulting me.

00:14:26.112 --> 00:14:29.309
You have no idea how much I can put up with.

00:14:30.051 --> 00:14:32.709
I'll prove to you that I can do it.

00:14:34.219 --> 00:14:36.269
She will adjust my schedule
and make sure I have time to train.

00:14:36.269 --> 00:14:40.029
My training schedule will be a bit different
for about a month.

00:14:44.719 --> 00:14:46.520
Do you have anything to say?

00:14:51.843 --> 00:14:53.644
You do it your way.

00:14:55.075 --> 00:14:56.876
I've got your back.

00:14:58.269 --> 00:15:00.184
What?

00:15:00.184 --> 00:15:01.985
What does it mean?

00:15:02.995 --> 00:15:05.629
It's an idiom.

00:15:07.107 --> 00:15:11.309
Like, I'll be here to help you out.

00:15:21.736 --> 00:15:23.414
Deal.

00:15:26.624 --> 00:15:27.933
Deal.

00:15:27.933 --> 00:15:30.421
Thank you so much. Thank you, thank you.

00:15:32.773 --> 00:15:35.309
You look like an inflatable tube man.

00:15:47.528 --> 00:15:49.549
Ms. Eva, I'm here to pick you up.

00:15:57.976 --> 00:16:00.271
She asked to see Ms. Eva only.

00:16:02.027 --> 00:16:06.109
She can't stay past six.
She has a meeting with the film producer.

00:16:07.285 --> 00:16:08.973
Let's go.

00:16:11.821 --> 00:16:14.749
Don't forget to send me your location
so I can pick you up later.

00:16:36.877 --> 00:16:38.678
Is she all right?

00:16:54.493 --> 00:16:56.309
Where are we heading to?

00:16:58.056 --> 00:17:00.869
She wanted to surprise you.

00:17:15.768 --> 00:17:19.269
Hey, she didn't tell me where we're going.

00:17:20.229 --> 00:17:23.149
Just keep giving me directions.
I'll follow you.

00:17:34.736 --> 00:17:36.869
They seemed pretty flustered.

00:17:37.643 --> 00:17:39.709
Who picked her up?

00:17:45.264 --> 00:17:46.549
- Hey.
- What?

00:17:46.549 --> 00:17:49.029
I saw her face before she left.

00:17:49.760 --> 00:17:51.730
She didn't look fine at all.

00:17:51.730 --> 00:17:53.997
She looked so anxious and scared.

00:17:53.997 --> 00:17:56.269
I know. I noticed that too.

00:17:56.269 --> 00:17:58.872
- She seemed so tense.
- Yeah.

00:17:58.872 --> 00:18:01.229
But I think she should be fine.

00:18:02.088 --> 00:18:03.688
What about this?

00:18:03.688 --> 00:18:07.347
Trust me,
let's just focus on our job and do our best.

00:18:07.347 --> 00:18:08.845
Okay?

00:18:08.845 --> 00:18:10.973
Can you look at this for me?

00:18:10.973 --> 00:18:13.605
When you're done, we can go.

00:18:13.605 --> 00:18:14.995
Sure.

00:18:14.995 --> 00:18:17.013
- You can go first.
- Why?

00:18:17.013 --> 00:18:19.120
I'll go check out some potential locations
to open a restaurant.

00:18:19.120 --> 00:18:21.232
My restaurant.

00:18:21.232 --> 00:18:23.029
- Wait, are you serious?
- I'm serious.

00:18:23.029 --> 00:18:25.370
- Do you want me to come with you?
- You don't have to.

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:26.789
I'll just look around.

00:18:26.789 --> 00:18:29.392
If I find the right place,
I'll ask for your help then.

00:18:29.392 --> 00:18:32.949
Sure. I'm glad you're doing this for yourself.

00:18:32.949 --> 00:18:35.819
Don't get so caught up in helping others
that you forget your own dreams.

00:18:35.819 --> 00:18:37.209
Okay?

00:19:35.786 --> 00:19:38.309
Eva, I'm on my way.

00:20:15.139 --> 00:20:17.229
Hello, Grandma.

00:20:18.829 --> 00:20:20.630
Follow me.

00:20:24.635 --> 00:20:27.349
Please leave your phone with me.

00:20:28.107 --> 00:20:30.368
Why do I have to?

00:20:30.368 --> 00:20:33.280
This feels threatening to me.

00:20:33.280 --> 00:20:34.712
Please leave your phone with me.

00:20:34.712 --> 00:20:36.878
It'll be easier to talk that way.

00:20:36.878 --> 00:20:39.229
She wants to keep this conversation private.

00:20:44.136 --> 00:20:47.029
It will be about campaign policies.

00:21:10.984 --> 00:21:13.715
This is my family's first home.

00:21:13.715 --> 00:21:17.429
We like to keep everything in order.

00:21:18.093 --> 00:21:22.060
We like it simple, and clean.

00:21:23.293 --> 00:21:25.312
You are famous.

00:21:25.312 --> 00:21:28.155
People are watching you.

00:21:28.155 --> 00:21:31.989
Even something small
can turn into a big issue.

00:21:34.315 --> 00:21:36.349
What are you trying to say?

00:21:36.965 --> 00:21:40.128
You need to conduct yourself
more professionally

00:21:40.128 --> 00:21:43.429
when you're helping my grandson
with his campaign.

00:21:47.835 --> 00:21:51.389
I'm upset about
how you've been behaving lately.

00:21:52.256 --> 00:21:57.149
After the party,
you didn't even come and apologize to me.

00:21:58.536 --> 00:22:01.349
I don't know how serious the argument was,

00:22:02.040 --> 00:22:04.949
but my grandson even bought you a car
as a peace offering.

00:22:06.315 --> 00:22:08.589
What bothered me the most was

00:22:09.675 --> 00:22:13.568
that you went running in the park
with another man,

00:22:13.568 --> 00:22:15.701
and photos of the two of you
ended up everywhere,

00:22:15.701 --> 00:22:20.229
even though you were dating my grandson.

00:22:21.037 --> 00:22:24.371
He's just my personal trainer, nothing more.

00:22:24.371 --> 00:22:27.149
I find that unacceptable.

00:22:28.144 --> 00:22:31.728
If the man you were running with
were better than my grandson,

00:22:31.728 --> 00:22:34.176
that would be a different story.

00:22:34.176 --> 00:22:36.869
But he's a nobody.

00:22:37.683 --> 00:22:41.331
My grandson had to buy you a car
because of that man,

00:22:41.331 --> 00:22:44.029
and you flaunted it all over social media.

00:22:45.475 --> 00:22:47.920
Weechana was the one who made me do it.

00:22:47.920 --> 00:22:49.675
You started it.

00:22:49.675 --> 00:22:53.269
Your behavior was disgraceful.

00:22:53.269 --> 00:22:57.109
So my grandson did what he had to do.

00:23:01.856 --> 00:23:07.109
Tomorrow, I want you to
focus on the campaign briefing.

00:23:08.288 --> 00:23:12.741
From now until the end of the campaign,

00:23:12.741 --> 00:23:15.309
I expect you to stay out of trouble

00:23:16.075 --> 00:23:19.269
and conduct yourself properly.

00:23:20.885 --> 00:23:22.907
I know

00:23:22.907 --> 00:23:27.429
you can't change your background
